# The rotation fold's cubins that have mined on a card with every hit verified, one line for each:
#   <toolkit release> <hash>
# The hash is the cubin's sha256 with its string table zeroed (python probes/hand89/asm89.py hash <cubin>).
# probes/hand89/build_rot.py refuses to write pearl_rot_sm89.cubin unless what it built is listed here for the
# toolkit that built it, and the host loads the file beside the core only when its hash is one of these
# (kRotCubins in pearl_host_rot.inc holds the same list). The loop in that file is written by hand, so a new
# line is added only after the file it names has run on an RTX 40 card: probes/verify-hits.js 400 of 400 with
# the fold on, and shares accepted. A line for a loop that is no longer built is taken out: its file may have
# another form of offsets records than this host writes.

# The loop of 12 November 2026: a gather's IADD3 and PRMT late, offsets records of 8 bytes, A's gathers early
# with the scoreboards chosen, a sixth quad (rfold.py al=1 bl=1 bp=1 co=1 ae=1 sbo=7 cq=35); and, RTX 40's own
# keys (build_rot.py's ARCH_KEYS), the readout's sums read as (0, 2) and (1, 3) on the chain of the other
# register parity, with U8 IMMA (rpr=2 u8=1), the readout's steps first in their gap (rgf=1) in a window of
# rb0=6 rb1=3; B drawn once for the two warps of a column slot, exchanged through the 16 KB that held the
# transcripts (bx=1 bsym=4 bsg=8 bsg3=24 bss=2 bord=2 barv=1 bxt=1; the transcript lives in the kernel's frame,
# ROT_BX=1); and records the eight warps share (sr=1, ROT_SR=1). The transcript store of the loop's tail holds its
# read scoreboard (without it a store queued behind the exchange stores could read R3 after the function's return
# zeroed it: an illegal address in repeated launches for some placements).

# CUDA 12.6 (rig01's local toolkit). rig01, RTX 4090: verify-hits 400 of 400 (742 hits, 19 salts, 810 MHz
# memory). By hashrate.js, alternating 120 s legs against the loop before it (e0e8a527..., records shared, B
# gathered by every warp): at 810 MHz memory 344.51, 344.38 and 344.37 TH/s against 343.03, 343.05 and 343.05;
# at the driver's memory clock 340.75, 340.79 and 340.61 against 339.15, 339.51 and 339.57. The probe's CPU
# check: 16,384 of 16,384 at k 2048, 8,192 of 8,192 at k 8192, 1,024 of 1,024 at k 65536, and 30 s runs (about 195 launches) clean in every placement that faulted before the fix.
12.6 3a354cac97eccf8716e74797850786b4f8e11e206351e5d296cc77b500d0bf49

# CUDA 12.8 (what CI builds with, Linux and Windows). The same code as 12.6's, byte for byte; the toolkit's
# version differs, in one byte of the ELF header and one of each kernel's .nv.info section. rig01, RTX 4090:
# verify-hits 400 of 400 (748 hits, 19 salts).
12.8 f1b1035e9e8c9a66086754139425e01e93e4f50990c864eee20ebb8f023e6ac8
